                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8dd0b61f-e929-4b6d-973a-9ef1c4a2ea4e",
                        "entry_id": "350e1492-4f7f-3846-9e78-4d82b3fd5389",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "thunderstruck"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "02526050-275d-496a-83fb-86c74ee2472c",
                        "entry_id": "350e1492-4f7f-3846-9e78-4d82b3fd5389",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "thunderstricken"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3a59f132-b41b-3259-8d08-67259bc5bd04",
                        "entry_id": "350e1492-4f7f-3846-9e78-4d82b3fd5389",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To strike, blast, or injure by, or as if by, lightning."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e24966d2-7ab4-48e9-ad45-2a6a016b4a86",
                                "sense_id": "3a59f132-b41b-3259-8d08-67259bc5bd04",
                                "text": "[…] some terrible bombarder of tearmes, as wilde as wildfire, that at the first flash of his fury, would leaue me thunder-stricken vpon the ground, or at the last volley of his outrage, would batter me to dust, and ashes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "131a4a3f-3042-4e71-b08c-07c71c8c8873",
                                "sense_id": "3a59f132-b41b-3259-8d08-67259bc5bd04",
                                "text": "1625, Samuel Purchas, Purchas His Pilgrimes, Part 3, London: Henrie Fetherstone, Book 4, Chapter 9, § 1, p. 738,\nAnd such Warres haue made impressions into all our Neighbour Countries […] haue lightened on Turkie and blasted the Seraglio; haue thunder-stricken Barbarie, haue torne the Atlas there,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "69849048-c1b4-4646-ab27-7a8852cffb1b",
                                "sense_id": "3a59f132-b41b-3259-8d08-67259bc5bd04",
                                "text": "[They] Seat God in the Clouds, and imagine his hands to be Employed, in opening and shutting the Cloisters of the Winds, in sprinkling the Flowers with dews, and thunder-striking the Tops of Mountains;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89c7e868-5e30-4847-a140-21f55fb52653",
                                "sense_id": "3a59f132-b41b-3259-8d08-67259bc5bd04",
                                "text": "1717, Joseph Addison (translator), Ovid’s Metamorphoses in Fifteen Books, London: Jacob Tonson, Book 2, “The Story of Phaeton,” p. 48,\nAt once from Life, and from the Chariot driv’n,\nTh’ ambitious Boy fell Thunder-struck from Heav’n."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a61f9b11-06b4-4151-be2b-798552879e8f",
                                "sense_id": "3a59f132-b41b-3259-8d08-67259bc5bd04",
                                "text": "The armaments which thunderstrike the walls\nOf rock-built cities, bidding nations quake,"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e7e9e800-82fe-3d2e-80ab-2a19147f6b84",
                        "entry_id": "350e1492-4f7f-3846-9e78-4d82b3fd5389",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To astonish, or strike dumb, as with something terrible."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "figuratively",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "142fe0ec-1774-40f8-bc55-6f55cd7231b1",
                                "sense_id": "e7e9e800-82fe-3d2e-80ab-2a19147f6b84",
                                "text": "At the expiration of this time, his lordship, who was already married, received a letter from his lady, who had been at the German Spa to drink the waters, intimating that she was on her return to England. This thunderstruck his lordship, who was sensible, that on her ladyship’s coming home, his new mistress must decamp."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6a23f8e-56cd-4d1b-8c59-6dcc99b6fed0",
                                "sense_id": "e7e9e800-82fe-3d2e-80ab-2a19147f6b84",
                                "text": "“Look, I tell you what, Mac. Seeing how as you're my best friend” “Yeah!” “Maybe you can look into it for me. Go snoop around the shop.” “Can-can I stop you for a second? I'm sorry. I'm a little confused here. You-you just said that he was your best friend? How is he your best friend over me?” “Well, I mean... You banged the waitress. Do I even have to explain that to you? That kind of rubbed me the wrong way, dude.” “Okay. I mean, you know, I don't see how that should factor into whether we're best friends or not. Y'know, to be honest with you, man, I'm a little shocked. I'm-I'm kinda-- I'm thunderstruck.” “Oh, well, I'm sorry, man. But y'know I didn't mean to hurt you. I didn't mean to thunderstrike you. But that's just-- I don't know what to tell you. What do you want to hear?” “I need for you to explain to me how it is that you consider Mac to be a better friend to you.” “Look, now this is just becoming awkward when I have a real problem! And all of a sudden it's about some weird feelings thing! And it's not about your feelings right now! It's about my feelings 'cause I have a problem, okay?. Now, Mac, please, do you think you can find this guy and kick his ass for me?”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e885b88f-3f18-4ec9-a523-b67bb529938d",
                        "source_entry_id": "350e1492-4f7f-3846-9e78-4d82b3fd5389",
                        "source_sense_description": "strike with lightning",
                        "target_lang_word": "foudroyer",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "foudroyer",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "12c5e4f7-2cab-32de-8684-d1695839a6dc",
                                        "entry_id": "7ccde69c-f76c-369f-87b6-5fd34456f228",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Frapper de la foudre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3efaa7ed-169c-4185-b5a8-6c76133eae1e",
                                                "sense_id": "12c5e4f7-2cab-32de-8684-d1695839a6dc",
                                                "text": "Les sabbats ont alors la forme grandiose et terrible de la Messe noire, de l’office à l’envers, où Jésus est défié, prié de foudroyer, s’il peut."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "677a2094-0a77-4d4a-81a2-f485ab6fce0e",
                                                "sense_id": "12c5e4f7-2cab-32de-8684-d1695839a6dc",
                                                "text": "En juillet 1926, le fils d'un cultivateur de Roizy (Ardennes), M. Surply et son ouvrier, M. Bertrand, étaient foudroyés dans les circonstances suivantes : Les deux hommes ramenant des champs un attelage chargé de foin, avaient été surpris par un orage à l'entrée du village et foudroyés, ainsi que les trois chevaux de l'attelage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48366685-0c01-323c-80e7-c3e242076fdf",
                                        "entry_id": "7ccde69c-f76c-369f-87b6-5fd34456f228",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Détruire à l’aide de canons, de bombes, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "analogy"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d5d3bcd-c00b-4685-9268-e48de46c0451",
                                                "sense_id": "48366685-0c01-323c-80e7-c3e242076fdf",
                                                "text": "Foudroyer une ville. — Le feu de la place foudroyait les assiégeants."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c04c692-8280-4e1e-971c-e536e2e30639",
                                                "sense_id": "48366685-0c01-323c-80e7-c3e242076fdf",
                                                "text": "Tout le vocabulaire qui servait jadis à la fois aux artilleurs et aux amants, on pouvait l’utiliser pour lui : Pierre mettait en batterie, démasquait, foudroyait, démontait."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ec384770-35c9-399e-afbc-fb875c3cb25b",
                                        "entry_id": "7ccde69c-f76c-369f-87b6-5fd34456f228",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Démolir un immeuble à l’explosif en le faisant tomber verticalement sur lui-même."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6947e51e-e55e-4522-93e9-a346e1d6a2d4",
                                                "sense_id": "ec384770-35c9-399e-afbc-fb875c3cb25b",
                                                "text": "Un grand \"boum\" et en une dizaine de secondes, la tour Kennedy n’était plus qu’une montagne de gravats. Il a fallu 800 kg d’explosifs pour foudroyer l’immeuble."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c969ca9-8f2d-395c-a100-856e828ad947",
                                        "entry_id": "7ccde69c-f76c-369f-87b6-5fd34456f228",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anéantir ou tuer rapidement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dc48c66-9bff-4069-99c1-e6a1d87df315",
                                                "sense_id": "2c969ca9-8f2d-395c-a100-856e828ad947",
                                                "text": "Ceux qui croient à un Dieu doivent se dire que, si leur Dieu ne foudroie pas les méchants, c’est qu’il voit la marche totale de son œuvre, et qu’il ne peut descendre au particulier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4df4f500-1677-437b-8321-01937e34cf43",
                                                "sense_id": "2c969ca9-8f2d-395c-a100-856e828ad947",
                                                "text": "Les loups me firent de loin une escorte. S’ils s’étaient rapprochés, je n’aurais pas résisté à la tentation d’en foudroyer un d’une balle bien placée. Peut-être, me disais-je, que cela calmerait les autres."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a56fd62d-c5ac-4f20-9576-5d9202e0184d",
                                                "sense_id": "2c969ca9-8f2d-395c-a100-856e828ad947",
                                                "text": "La balle unique avait touché le fauve, mais sans le foudroyer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87f29a87-c82c-4997-afb8-b1fc0365d013",
                                                "sense_id": "2c969ca9-8f2d-395c-a100-856e828ad947",
                                                "text": "Mais à Babylone, en 323, la maladie foudroie le jeune souverain qui meurt à trente-trois ans, tout auréolé de gloire. Alexandre a donné naissance à une monarchie universelle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a772d4f3-fecc-3e4e-a231-4ad1c166a768",
                                        "entry_id": "7ccde69c-f76c-369f-87b6-5fd34456f228",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Terrasser ; interdire ; confondre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a858aef6-b8b9-4581-b20e-352147d78029",
                                                "sense_id": "a772d4f3-fecc-3e4e-a231-4ad1c166a768",
                                                "text": "Il eut un mouvement furieux pour s'élancer sur Giselle. Mais il s'arrêta, foudroyé par le regard de Marie de Médicis qui lui disait : \"Monsieur le maréchal, vous voudrez bien m'apporter un rapport sur la conspiration et nous tiendrons conseil.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4272581-37da-42d1-874b-608010784bda",
                                                "sense_id": "a772d4f3-fecc-3e4e-a231-4ad1c166a768",
                                                "text": "Son visage eût été agréable sans le regard des yeux bleus qui foudroyaient les dîneurs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79c15611-15e3-3af9-8050-48c90d114e26",
                                        "entry_id": "7ccde69c-f76c-369f-87b6-5fd34456f228",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Combattre avec véhémence ; stigmatiser avec éloquence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ef7360f-b606-4133-8c6b-f36fc30dcf8f",
                                                "sense_id": "79c15611-15e3-3af9-8050-48c90d114e26",
                                                "text": "Cet orateur a foudroyé ses adversaires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69f3d4da-9bf3-4254-b6f6-eccd403ebca8",
                                                "sense_id": "79c15611-15e3-3af9-8050-48c90d114e26",
                                                "text": "Cet argument le foudroya. — Foudroyer les erreurs, les vices, etc."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fa5ae67-c25d-417c-acdc-18a8ab986b48",
                                                "sense_id": "79c15611-15e3-3af9-8050-48c90d114e26",
                                                "text": "De l’apprendre de cette façon m’a proprement foudroyé."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ad953e7e-157f-47f4-b4aa-82211a573427",
